NAME
    snake - the classic snake game

SYNOPSIS
    snake

DESCRIPTION
    A snake crawls around a walled board and grows every time it eats.
    The arrow keys steer it, and it dies when it runs into a wall or
    into its own body. Each meal is ten points and the snake moves a
    little faster with every one, down to a floor the eye can still
    follow.

    The board is a grid of 30 by 20 cells and the window opens at
    exactly that size; a status line under it shows the score and the
    best score of the session.

    A snake cannot reverse into its own neck: a turn that would send it
    straight back the way it came is ignored. Only the last turn counts
    between two steps, so a quick double turn arrives as one.

    The game is a desktop app, so it lives under /apps/snake and has a
    tile on the desktop; the shell can start it like any command. Like
    every window it is closed with Esc, and its score is not kept once
    the window is gone.

KEYS
    Up, Down, Left, Right   steer the snake
    p                       pause, and again to resume
    Space                   start a new game, once the snake is dead
    Esc                     close the window
